Local experiment hook, not for upstream: let the environment override the ISP
noise-reduction strength that setParameters() derived from the AIQ results.

The HAL's own presets map onto the same scale: NR_LEVEL4 = -120, NR_LEVEL3 =
-60, and the default NR_LEVEL2 leaves strength at 0. Hardware-verified on the
HP EliteBook X G2i (OV05C10, 2026-08-30): HPCAM_NR_STRENGTH=-60 cuts
within-frame dark-scene noise ~28%, -120 ~45%, with no visible detail smearing
at -120. The daemon in hp-elitebook-x-g2i-camera exports the knob to the
CamHAL subprocess; unset, the HAL behaves exactly as unpatched.

Applies to intel/ipu7-camera-hal tag 20260327_1 (58e6f01f).

diff --git a/src/core/ProcessingUnit.cpp b/src/core/ProcessingUnit.cpp
index 5b29d8c..1a4b224 100644
--- a/src/core/ProcessingUnit.cpp
+++ b/src/core/ProcessingUnit.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 
 #include "ProcessingUnit.h"
 
+#include <cstdlib>
 #include <set>
 #include <utility>
 
@@ -261,6 +262,11 @@ int ProcessingUnit::setParameters(const DataContext* dataContext) {
             = static_cast<char>(dataContext->mIspParams.nrLevel.nrLevel.overall);
     }
 
+    // Local experiment hook (not for upstream): override NR strength via env.
+    if (const char* envNr = ::getenv("HPCAM_NR_STRENGTH")) {
+        mIspSettings.nrSetting.strength = static_cast<char>(::atoi(envNr));
+    }
+
     LOG2("%s: ISP NR setting, level: %d, strength: %d", __func__,
          static_cast<int>(mIspSettings.nrSetting.feature_level),
          static_cast<int>(mIspSettings.nrSetting.strength));
